meaning:
Cartier is an affluential French luxury company known for their jewelry and watches, founded by Louis-François Cartier in 1847. Worn by several prominent figures such as Duchess of Cambridge Kate Middleton, Cartier has established itself as one of the world’s leading jewelry brands.



This verse is a double entendre, serving as a both a nod to Uzi’s 2016 song, “Cartier”, and his love for the business and its glasses. Uzi references his Cartier eyewear in many of his songs, a prime example being in his 2016 track, “Team Rocket”;

Cartier all on my face

Chanel is a stellar luxury fashion company founded by Coco Chanel in 1909 based in Paris, France. Known for their various perfumes, handbags, and jewelry, prestigious artists like Lil Uzi Vert and Young Thug have recently introduced sneakers and from the group to the rap industry.



In Uzi and Pharrell William’s 2017 track, “Neon Guts”, Uzi also threw in a reference about the exquisite brand;

I put Chanel on my shooter

Visvim is a luxurious designer company founded by Hiroki Nakamura in the fashion district of Ura-Harajuku, Japan in 2001. The brand is known for their exceptional footwear.



Lil Uzi Vert in Visvims.

Uzi has shown to be very into the shoes, and has mentioned them in several of his tracks, such as his 2017 song, “3 Pills”;

These are not Jordans, these Visvims;

The Philadelphia native uses a play on words in the first and latter part of the verse, as “visvims” and “vision” sound alike.
